      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The FDA-approved label for sertraline sets a maximum of 200 mg/day for all indications. 1000 mg is 5 times that limit, so I can't enter it as within label.\n\nI'm not doubting you personally. I can't verify the clinical context, and a dose this far above the maximum could seriously harm the patient. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, or cardiac toxicity.\n\nWhat I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the label range.** For example, 50 mg or 100 mg by mouth once daily, up to 200 mg/day. Tell me which.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or the attending.** If you think the patient needs more than 200 mg/day, they can review it and follow your institution's process for an off-label order. That process is the way to get a dose like this placed.\n\nIf there's a different drug or dose behind this, such as a typo or a mix-up with another medication, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order."
      }
